# Local-only worker vars for `wrangler dev`. Copy this file to `.dev.vars`
# (gitignored) before your first `pnpm dev`:
#
#     cp apps/scena/.dev.vars.example apps/scena/.dev.vars
#
# Wrangler loads `.dev.vars` automatically for `wrangler dev` ONLY. It is never
# uploaded by `wrangler deploy`.

# ── The dev lane switch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `ENVIRONMENT=development` is the single explicit signal that this worker is a
# throwaway local one. It is what lets `@4dl/auth` start without a real
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (outside development it REFUSES to start rather than sign
# sessions with a key that is public in this repo), and what the mock email
# provider reads before logging a sign-in code to the console instead of failing
# closed.
ENVIRONMENT=development

# ── DANGER: never move this into wrangler.jsonc ──────────────────────────────
# `wrangler.jsonc`'s top-level `vars` block IS the deployed configuration. If
# `ENVIRONMENT: "development"` is added there it ships to production: sessions
# signed with a forgeable key, and sign-in codes written to retained logs.
# Keep this variable in `.dev.vars` only.

# ── Optional local overrides ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment to test the real Better Auth signing path locally (otherwise the
# dev fallback key is used):
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=run-openssl-rand-base64-32-and-paste-here
